  "result": "Excellent! All 119 tests pass. Here's a summary of the VAT implementation:\n\n## VAT Implementation Summary\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n**1. Core VAT Functions (src/invoices.js)**\n- Added `lineVAT(line)` function:\n  - Calculates VAT on the line amount **after discount** is applied\n  - Formula: `(lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100`\n  - Rounded per line using `roundCents()`\n  - Clamped at 0 (never negative)\n\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`:\n  - `subtotal` = sum of all line totals (before discount/VAT)\n  - `discount` = sum of all line discounts\n  - `vat` = sum of all line VATs (each calculated on discounted amount)\n  - `total` = subtotal - discount + vat (clamped at 0)\n\n**2. Invoice Rendering (src/render.js)**\n- Updated `renderInvoiceText()` to show VAT on its own line:\n  - Displays \"VAT: \u20acXXX.XX\" just above the total (only when VAT > 0)\n  - VAT line appears after line items, before total\n\n**3. Test Coverage (26 new VAT tests)**\n- Per-line VAT calculations with different rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n- VAT rounding accuracy\n- Combined discount + VAT scenarios\n- Tier discount + VAT combinations\n- Mixed VAT rates on single invoice\n- Render output with VAT displayed\n\n### Key Design Decisions:\n- **VAT on discounted amount**: VAT is calculated per line on `(lineTotal - lineDiscount)`, not on full line total\n- **Per-line rounding**: Each line's VAT is rounded independently, then summed\n- **Clamping at zero**: All amounts (discount, VAT, total) never go below zero\n- **Zero VAT display**: VAT line only shown when total VAT > 0 (cleaner rendering for exempt items)\n\n**All 119 tests passing** \u2713",
